-- =====================================================================================
-- ClassLess -- the whole custom dataset, in load order.
--
-- GENERATED by tools/classless-web/merge_sql.py from the individual classless_*.sql files.
-- Regenerate rather than hand-editing: each part still has its own generator, and this is
-- only the concatenation plus the order they have to run in.
--
-- Re-runnable end to end. Every part is DELETE+INSERT or a fixed-value UPDATE, so applying
-- this file twice lands on the same state.
--
-- Applied automatically: this file lives in data/sql/custom/db_world, one of the directories
-- AzerothCore's updater scans, and the updater re-runs a file whose hash has changed -- which
-- every regeneration does. Applying it by hand still works and is what --verify does:
--
--     mysql -uacore -pacore acore_world < zz_classless.sql
--
-- The "zz_" prefix is part of the load order, not decoration. Every .sql the updater can see --
-- core updates, the custom directories and every enabled module's data/sql -- goes into ONE list
-- sorted by FILENAME, with the directory ignored. Several mod-individual-progression files wipe a
-- creature's loot wholesale (DELETE FROM creature_loot_template WHERE Entry = 7369, in
-- zone_deadwind_pass.sql), so this dataset has to sort after them or its rows are deleted right
-- after being written.
--
-- ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. Three dependencies are not obvious:
--
--   * classless_rank_items.sql recreates the tome rows with RequiredLevel 0, so the
--     required-level pass has to come after it, not before.
--   * the loot table is emitted whole by classless_tome_loot.sql; the rare-buff and
--     starter-cleanup passes carve rows back OUT of it, so they follow it.
--   * chances and conditions are keyed to rows that exist, so they run last.
--
-- NOT INCLUDED, on purpose. The superseded ones now live in custom/superseded/ so that
-- applying the folder in filename order cannot revert this file:

--   * the layered loot builds                classless_rank_loot{,_replace,_retheme,_srcfix}.sql, classless_alt_tomes_loot.sql, classless_tomes_loot{,_fix}.sql -- five passes over a per-row placement that classless_group_loot.sql now emits in one
--   * the per-row loot successors            classless_tome_loot.sql, _chances.sql, _conditions.sql -- superseded in their turn when the group rule replaced per-row placement on 2026-09-13
--   * patches on generated item columns      classless_tome_use_spell_fix.sql, classless_rank_required_level.sql, classless_tome_quality_floor.sql -- rank_items.py emits every one of those columns itself
--   * the npc_casts generation               classless_npc_casts.sql, _retire.sql, classless_tome_icons.sql -- classless_npc_showcast.sql owns the same smart_scripts id band and opens with the same unfiltered DELETE
--   * one-shot migrations                    rev_1786654338394442900.sql halved every loot chance on EACH run; classless_drop_panel_columns.sql is a DROP COLUMN; ahbot_account_character.sql hard-coded the AH bot at guid 1
-- =====================================================================================


-- #####################################################################################
-- ## RETIRED CONTENT
-- #####################################################################################

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- classless_retired.sql
-- clears every id block ClassLess no longer uses, in one file: the one-tome-per-LINE items (60000-61999), the 21 proficiency manuals (62000-62099) and the hint notes (73000-76999), each with its loot, vendor and condition rows. A no-op on a realm built from zero; it earns its place on one that has been running since before the retirements
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ClassLess: everything the design no longer uses, cleared in one place.
--
-- This replaces four files that each cleared one retired id block
-- (classless_tomes_items, classless_hint_items_retired, classless_prof_retire,
-- classless_starter_loot_cleanup). They were separate because each retirement happened on its
-- own day; there was never a reason for them to stay separate afterwards, and four files that
-- all say DELETE made the merge plan look like it had four decisions in it instead of one.
--
-- WHAT THIS IS FOR. On a realm built from zero it is a no-op: no generator emits any of these
-- entries, so nothing ever creates them. It earns its place on a realm that has been running
-- since before the retirements, where the rows are still sitting in the tables -- and a loot row
-- pointing at an item that no longer exists is a warning LootMgr logs once per kill, forever.
--
-- Re-runnable, and scoped strictly to id blocks ClassLess owns.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 60000-61999 -- one tome per ABILITY LINE (560 spells + 622 talents).
--
-- Superseded by classless_rank_items.sql, which seeds one tome per ABILITY RANK at 63000-66999.
-- Removed outright rather than left in place: the legacy-unlock branch is gone from
-- Server.lua and tomes.data, and every owned instance (bots only) was purged from
-- item_instance / character_inventory / mail_items at the time.
--
-- The loot DELETE is a range where it used to be a generated list of 108 ids
-- (classless_starter_loot_cleanup.sql, written when these items still existed, to stop the
-- starter lines dropping a tome that could only ever say "You already know this ability").
-- Once the items themselves were gone, every row in the block was an orphan, so the id list
-- was a narrower way of saying the same thing and needed a generator to stay correct.
DELETE FROM `creature_loot_template` WHERE `Item` BETWEEN 60000 AND 61999;
DELETE FROM `npc_vendor`             WHERE `item` BETWEEN 60000 AND 61999;
DELETE FROM `conditions` WHERE `SourceTypeOrReferenceId` = 1
                           AND `SourceEntry` BETWEEN 60000 AND 61999;
DELETE FROM `item_template`          WHERE `entry` BETWEEN 60000 AND 61999;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 62000-62099 -- the 21 collectible weapon/armour proficiency manuals.
--
-- Retired 2026-09-11. Every character now has all 21 proficiencies from level one, applied by
-- Server.lua's ApplyProficiencies on login at skill 1 with a ceiling of 75, so there is nothing
-- left to collect. The argument for not putting them back: proficiency is the FLOOR of the game,
-- not a reward in it. Without armour proficiency a character cannot equip anything at all, so a
-- manual was a prerequisite dressed as a collectible -- and until profspread.py moved them, nine
-- of the primaries stood inside dungeons, which asked a level 5 character to find a group for the
-- right to hold a mace.
DELETE FROM `creature_loot_template` WHERE `Item` BETWEEN 62000 AND 62099;
DELETE FROM `npc_vendor`             WHERE `item` BETWEEN 62000 AND 62099;
DELETE FROM `conditions` WHERE `SourceTypeOrReferenceId` = 1
                           AND `SourceEntry` BETWEEN 62000 AND 62099;
DELETE FROM `item_template`          WHERE `entry` BETWEEN 62000 AND 62099;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 73000-76999 -- the "Weathered Notes: <ability>" hint items, one per rank at tome id + 10000.
--
-- They dropped at a flat 2% on every kill and carried their pointer in the item description. Each
-- cost a bag slot and only cleared itself when that exact rank was learned, so a character
-- levelling to 80 accumulated dozens. The note was a nudge, not something worth paying for in
-- inventory space every session.
--
-- 500782 was their icon in itemdisplayinfo_dbc, used by these items and nothing else. The tome
-- display rows (500000-500781) stay: they belong to the tomes.
DELETE FROM `creature_loot_template` WHERE `Item` BETWEEN 73000 AND 76999;
DELETE FROM `npc_vendor`             WHERE `item` BETWEEN 73000 AND 76999;
DELETE FROM `conditions` WHERE `SourceTypeOrReferenceId` = 1
                           AND `SourceEntry` BETWEEN 73000 AND 76999;
DELETE FROM `item_template`          WHERE `entry` BETWEEN 73000 AND 76999;
DELETE FROM `itemdisplayinfo_dbc`    WHERE `ID` = 500782;


-- #####################################################################################
-- ## ITEM DISPLAY ROWS (DBC OVERRIDE)
-- #####################################################################################

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- classless_tomes_display.sql
-- itemdisplayinfo_dbc 500000-500781, used by every rank tome
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ClassLess tomes: item display rows, one per distinct ability icon.
--
-- GENERATED by tools/classless-web/rank_items.py -- regenerate, do not hand-edit.
--
-- The matching client-side rows ship in the patch MPQ as ItemDisplayInfo.dbc; these are the
-- server's copy, via AzerothCore's DBC override table. Icon art is NOT shipped: every leaf
-- name below is an icon the client already has, because the spellbook already draws it.
--
-- Ids are never renumbered: the client reads the matching row from the patch MPQ, so a moved
-- id is a tome drawing the wrong picture. New art is added at the end, in both places at once.


DELETE FROM `itemdisplayinfo_dbc` WHERE `ID` BETWEEN 500000 AND 500781;


