-- Creatures an earlier placement pointed at their own lootid and this one does not
-- use. Left alone they keep an empty loot table, which worldserver reports at startup
-- and LootMgr reports again on every kill. The guards are in the statement, not in a
-- query, so re-applying this file cannot wear them away: `lootid` = `entry` never
-- touches a creature pointing at a shared table, and NOT EXISTS zeroes an id only
-- while it still names nothing.
